1
00:00:13,763 --> 00:00:14,597
FASTER

2
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:18,184
MORE

3
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:21,604
CHEAPER

4
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:27,819
ACHIEVE 150% OF TARGET

5
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:45,754
Let's eat and continue!

6
00:00:45,837 --> 00:00:48,923
Over here, finish up and go, you hear?

7
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:50,925
Meet the quota, or it's overtime today!

8
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:02,937
Yeon-joo.

9
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,149
Let's eat first.

10
00:01:07,984 --> 00:01:08,985
Okay.

11
00:01:09,736 --> 00:01:11,071
- I'm so hungry.
- Right?

12
00:01:11,154 --> 00:01:13,114
- Let's dig in.
- Let's eat.

13
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:15,533
- Enjoy your meal.
- Enjoy your meal.

14
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:18,578
Yeon-joo.

15
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:22,207
A young lady should have
better side dishes than that.

16
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:24,417
You even used to be a maid.

17
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:27,670
Who has time to cook?

18
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:30,006
Or the money to buy groceries?

19
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:33,301
It tastes fine to me.

20
00:01:33,384 --> 00:01:35,845
That's because
you send all your salary home.

21
00:01:36,346 --> 00:01:40,350
You frugal little thing. Yeon-joo,
you're really going to do well in life.

22
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:43,103
- Where were you?
- Have you guys heard?

23
00:01:43,978 --> 00:01:45,647
Our union president.

24
00:01:46,731 --> 00:01:50,401
- I heard he sided with the company.
- What? Yeong-chun did?

25
00:01:53,696 --> 00:01:55,990
- I knew that bastard looked shady.
- No, but…

26
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:58,368
Then,

27
00:01:59,452 --> 00:02:00,578
what about us?

28
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:05,542
What happens to us?
Are we going to continue?

29
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:06,835
Yeon-joo.

30
00:02:07,877 --> 00:02:10,338
We're human beings, not machines.

31
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:14,050
If they stomp us to death,
we have to retaliate.

32
00:02:15,426 --> 00:02:16,553
Because we're alive.

33
00:02:18,012 --> 00:02:19,639
- It looks delicious.
- Right?

34
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:23,726
- Hey!
- Give it here!

35
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:25,436
- Everyone, run!
- Get her!

36
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:26,479
Run!

37
00:02:26,563 --> 00:02:27,647
- Come here!
- What's up?

38
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:29,607
You factory girls dare incite a riot?

39
00:02:30,483 --> 00:02:32,110
- Let's go.
- Goddammit.

40
00:02:32,193 --> 00:02:33,945
- You fucking bitch, let go!
- Hurry!

41
00:02:34,028 --> 00:02:36,239
- Get inside, hurry!
- Oh no.

42
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:38,241
- Give it here!
- Get inside, hurry!

43
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:41,411
You fucking bitches, take these all down!

44
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:43,746
- Run!
- You're all fired!

45
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:45,039
- Hurry up!
- Run!

46
00:02:45,123 --> 00:02:46,291
Hurry!

47
00:02:47,917 --> 00:02:49,919
This is absolute nonsense!

48
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:50,897
DEAD-END JOB

49
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:55,026
NEO WORLD AFTER DARK

50
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:14,796
What the…

51
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:23,805
Why are you here?

52
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:35,066
I can't reach that weird woman,
and the owner here won't tell me shit.

53
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:36,192
Well, you see…

54
00:04:38,569 --> 00:04:39,404
Sorry.

55
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,490
God, seriously.

56
00:04:44,742 --> 00:04:47,704
You're alive, so it's fine, but--

57
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:52,292
Come on in.

58
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:06,055
128,384,000 won.

59
00:05:08,474 --> 00:05:09,309
Here you go.

60
00:05:09,392 --> 00:05:11,060
One hundred million…

61
00:05:12,061 --> 00:05:14,105
You'll need a bag too.

62
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:16,649
The bag's on the house.

63
00:05:39,088 --> 00:05:40,590
Let's go.

64
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:41,716
See you again.

65
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:48,348
- I'd like to ask--
- Don't ever give Hyeok-jun a job again.

66
00:05:50,516 --> 00:05:53,811
If there's no demand, there's no supply.

67
00:05:55,271 --> 00:05:56,397
There's no demand, right?

68
00:05:57,523 --> 00:05:59,776
- What?
- Tell me. Is there demand or not?

69
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:02,820
No, there isn't.

70
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:03,946
You got that?

71
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:06,199
Let's go.

72
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:14,332
Shit, this is crazy! How much is this?
This isn't a dream, right?

73
00:06:19,212 --> 00:06:20,213
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

74
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:23,424
Who needs a famous restaurant?

75
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:26,219
Mom, eat up. The meat's done.

76
00:06:26,302 --> 00:06:28,137
And you slow down, jeez.

77
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:30,181
Why you gotta be like that with food?

78
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:34,018
Did paying off your debt
give you some breathing room?

79
00:06:35,144 --> 00:06:37,355
Debt? What are you talking about?

80
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:41,150
- What debt do you have?
- I don't. I paid it all off.

81
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:42,819
Mom, he lost everything in stocks.

82
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:44,153
Stocks?

83
00:06:45,154 --> 00:06:47,990
What money did you have
to invest in stocks?

84
00:06:48,991 --> 00:06:50,034
Well, see…

85
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:53,746
You little punk,
how could you be so reckless?

86
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:54,956
What about your place?

87
00:06:55,039 --> 00:06:58,334
- What about the <i>jeonse </i>deposit?
- It's still there! I didn't touch it!

88
00:06:58,418 --> 00:07:01,379
- Ji-yoon, is he telling the truth?
- Yes, he is.

89
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:08,386
Mom, I swear. I put everything on the line
and worked hard to pay off all my debt.

90
00:07:08,469 --> 00:07:10,096
Don't worry.

91
00:07:10,179 --> 00:07:11,305
For goodness' sake.

92
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,184
That damn debt.

93
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:18,604
When I think about
how I spent my whole life on edge

94
00:07:19,188 --> 00:07:20,606
because of your father…

95
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:24,026
Mom, are you drunk?

96
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:27,530
You always talk about absent people
when you drink. Stop it.

97
00:07:27,613 --> 00:07:29,740
That's not what I'm saying.

98
00:07:33,202 --> 00:07:34,203
It's because of money

99
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:37,039
that your father ended up like that.

100
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,585
I just feel so bad for him.

101
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:48,968
I think my dad worked part-time
at a construction site too.

102
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:52,889
So I went to one too.

103
00:07:53,931 --> 00:07:55,766
That's where I heard about a door.

104
00:07:58,144 --> 00:08:00,313
What do you want to do?

105
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:01,355
Well,

106
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,275
I want to find him.

107
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,321
If he's alive, that is.

108
00:08:10,781 --> 00:08:12,825
But I guess there's no hope, right?

109
00:08:13,409 --> 00:08:15,244
It's been 20 years.

110
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:19,081
Well,

111
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:21,501
it's not impossible.

112
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:24,712
If he crossed over
to the other world alive.

113
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,090
As you heard,

114
00:08:28,841 --> 00:08:30,676
the part-time job locations

115
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:34,764
have a door that leads to the other world.

116
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:41,020
And vice versa.
There's a door that leads back here.

117
00:08:42,438 --> 00:08:43,856
A door?

118
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:46,400
The only door I know of

119
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,070
is at an amusement park.

120
00:08:53,908 --> 00:08:56,911
How do you know that?

121
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:00,665
Because I came back through that door

122
00:09:01,165 --> 00:09:02,375
from the other world.

123
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:05,503
<i>Yellow flowers</i>
<i>Even when the garden is in full bloom</i>

124
00:09:05,586 --> 00:09:09,632
<i>White butterflies, flower butterflies</i>
<i>Even when they flutter over the wall</i>

125
00:09:09,715 --> 00:09:10,967
<i>The warm spring breeze…</i>

126
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:12,885
<i>- It was 40 years ago.</i>
- What fine singers!

127
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:14,220
Turn on the lights!

128
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:26,482
<i>At first, I thought</i>
<i>I could change the world.</i>

129
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,487
Drag them out!

130
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,574
Get out here! Drag them out!

131
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:38,202
Come out! Where the hell are they?

132
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:39,954
Come out, damn it!

133
00:09:40,538 --> 00:09:41,581
You little…

134
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:43,082
Drag them all out!

135
00:09:43,165 --> 00:09:45,543
Bring that bitch over here!

136
00:09:46,043 --> 00:09:48,045
You come over here!

137
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:48,963
You come here!

138
00:09:51,632 --> 00:09:53,134
Hurry!

139
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:57,138
Get in here.

140
00:09:58,097 --> 00:09:59,432
Drag them out now!

141
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:00,766
Hide here until it's over.

142
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:02,351
No, I…

143
00:10:02,852 --> 00:10:08,024
Yeon-joo, go out there and tell the world.
It's the only way we can change it.

144
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:12,737
Drag them out right now!

145
00:10:14,905 --> 00:10:16,032
You're dead today.

146
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:18,576
- I'll take this shovel…
- Let go! Let go of me!

147
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:21,037
Come here.

148
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:26,500
Let go of me!

149
00:10:32,506 --> 00:10:34,884
<i>I'm not sure how much time had passed…</i>

150
00:10:40,431 --> 00:10:43,100
<i>but when I finally opened the door</i>…

151
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:10,294
<i>I saw that the textile factory</i>

152
00:11:11,212 --> 00:11:13,297
<i>had been turned into an amusement park.</i>

153
00:11:24,517 --> 00:11:28,020
FANTASY HAUNTED HOUSE

154
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:32,692
No one remembered me.

155
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:39,990
That's a terrifying thing.

156
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:45,830
Your father

157
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:48,791
might also be waiting

158
00:11:49,291 --> 00:11:50,793
for someone to find him.

159
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:55,631
I'll help you find your father.

160
00:12:09,895 --> 00:12:10,855
Hey!

161
00:12:11,355 --> 00:12:12,523
Mr. Hyeok-jun!

162
00:12:14,525 --> 00:12:16,569
You're here.

163
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:19,405
I was hoping you'd come.

164
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:21,449
Come in.

165
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:25,995
Let's see. Jobs for today…

166
00:12:28,748 --> 00:12:30,040
Byeon Min-su.

167
00:12:32,001 --> 00:12:33,669
He did these jobs.

168
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:41,010
You sent me to the construction site
because you know who he is.

169
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:47,725
As I told you before,
I don't know who he is.

170
00:12:48,267 --> 00:12:49,101
You know him…

171
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:53,439
but you can't say. Am I right?

172
00:12:56,025 --> 00:12:57,485
You don't have to answer that.

173
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:01,071
Instead, give me the amusement park job.

174
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:05,326
The amusement park?

175
00:13:06,535 --> 00:13:08,162
How did you know about that?

176
00:13:27,556 --> 00:13:28,891
Are you sure about this?

177
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:31,727
Barely anyone's succeeded.

178
00:13:33,437 --> 00:13:35,189
This part-time job can turn full-time.

179
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:39,276
Full-time?

180
00:13:39,777 --> 00:13:41,987
If you become a full-time employee…

181
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:48,244
you might learn what you're eager to know.

182
00:14:06,470 --> 00:14:09,890
ACCEPT

183
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:12,977
Just get through--

184
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:15,980
I'll just get through the day.

185
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:22,069
BYEON JI-YOON
THINK I DID WELL AT THE INTERVIEW TODAY

186
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:27,533
WILL COME OVER AFTER MEETING A FRIEND
WANT ME TO BRING SOME FRIED CHICKEN?

187
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:45,634
IF ANYTHING HAPPENS, TELL MOM…

188
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:56,854
THE INTERVIEW WENT WELL,
SO LET'S HAVE SOME FRIED CHICKEN

189
00:14:56,937 --> 00:15:03,944
I HAVE PLANS TOO, SO I'LL BE HOME LATE
SEE YOU TONIGHT

190
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:08,574
WELCOME TO THE JOY-FILLED NEO WORLD!

191
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:31,347
This is the door.

192
00:15:34,975 --> 00:15:36,602
This one?

193
00:15:37,102 --> 00:15:39,605
This is the door?

194
00:15:40,689 --> 00:15:41,523
Yes.

195
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:43,651
The door I came out of.

196
00:15:52,242 --> 00:15:54,828
It's just a storage room.

197
00:15:57,289 --> 00:15:59,166
It won't be when you work at night.

198
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:09,760
<i>It won't be easy to get to the door.</i>

199
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:13,430
<i>Act normal while you work</i>
<i>and bide your time.</i>

200
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:22,272
It's definitely different from the day.

201
00:16:40,499 --> 00:16:41,333
What the…?

202
00:16:46,463 --> 00:16:48,007
What the hell?

203
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:54,179
Excuse me?

204
00:16:58,350 --> 00:17:01,353
Is anyone here?
I'm here for the part-time job.

205
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:05,482
Fucking hell.

206
00:17:17,661 --> 00:17:19,079
Do you work here?

207
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:22,875
I'm here for--

208
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:27,046
Please come this way.

209
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:30,007
The others are already here.

210
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:34,136
Shall we go?

211
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:39,058
One, two, three, four.

212
00:17:44,605 --> 00:17:45,814
Follow along.

213
00:17:50,235 --> 00:17:57,242
One, two, three, four…

214
00:17:58,994 --> 00:18:05,501
One, two, three, four…

215
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:12,591
One, two, three, four…
Two, two, three, four…

216
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:17,679
One, two, three, four… One--

217
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:18,597
Stop!

218
00:18:21,975 --> 00:18:22,851
Wolf.

219
00:18:23,393 --> 00:18:24,728
Put on your head mask.

220
00:18:27,606 --> 00:18:29,066
Okay.

221
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:41,328
Standing here like this,
we all know which fable this is, right?

222
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:44,957
That's right.
It's "The Three Little Pigs."

223
00:18:49,586 --> 00:18:52,047
Okay, then, Wolf.

224
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:54,633
What should you do?

225
00:18:55,592 --> 00:18:59,388
Chase after the three little pigs?

226
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:09,940
That's correct.
That's the only thing the wolf has to do.

227
00:19:11,191 --> 00:19:13,777
Wolves don't talk like people, do they?

228
00:19:19,074 --> 00:19:20,742
- Shall we try it right now?
- Sure.

229
00:19:24,371 --> 00:19:25,289
Cue

230
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:26,999
the music.

231
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:33,714
Feel free to improvise!

232
00:19:36,508 --> 00:19:38,218
You must catch them, Wolf!

233
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:43,390
Damn it.

234
00:19:46,810 --> 00:19:47,978
Go, Wolf!

235
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:57,946
Who are these people?

236
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:02,993
Shall we switch up the mood?

237
00:20:03,076 --> 00:20:04,912
Cue the music!

238
00:20:07,956 --> 00:20:08,790
Holy…

239
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:12,920
Damn.

240
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:17,549
What are you…

241
00:20:23,263 --> 00:20:25,641
Now it's the pigs' turn.

242
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:33,398
Byeon Hyeok-jun,
I brought fried chicken. Get out here.

243
00:20:35,442 --> 00:20:36,735
Oh, right.

244
00:20:37,444 --> 00:20:38,862
He said he had plans.

245
00:20:55,545 --> 00:20:56,380
Wait.

246
00:20:57,547 --> 00:20:58,924
Why's it so clean?

247
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:39,172
CONVENIENCE STORE, MANAGER, MILK DELIVERY
CLINICAL TRIAL, CONSTRUCTION SITE

248
00:21:43,427 --> 00:21:44,803
"Find Dad"?

249
00:21:46,388 --> 00:21:48,307
No, wait!

250
00:21:51,059 --> 00:21:53,270
Wait, you said I was the villain!

251
00:21:53,353 --> 00:21:55,939
Forget the old fable
of the chased little pigs.

252
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:58,150
Now it's time to hunt the wolf.

253
00:21:58,233 --> 00:21:59,276
Shit.

254
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:17,544
Enough!

255
00:22:18,086 --> 00:22:20,630
Enough.

256
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:25,302
You got him.

257
00:22:25,385 --> 00:22:27,721
You did a great job, little pigs.

258
00:22:27,804 --> 00:22:28,847
Rehearsal is over!

259
00:22:34,394 --> 00:22:35,937
This is batshit insane.

260
00:22:38,982 --> 00:22:41,985
Staged role-play is all about image.
Never unmask while working.

261
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:43,820
Without your head, you're fair game.

262
00:22:45,238 --> 00:22:49,618
The wolf must put more heart into it
during the real thing.

263
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:51,536
Okay.

264
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:53,497
And don't use human language.

265
00:22:54,456 --> 00:22:56,541
Now, shall we go on to the parade?

266
00:22:58,001 --> 00:23:05,008
Right, left…

267
00:23:05,092 --> 00:23:07,260
All right, let's hit the road!

268
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:12,516
March in step, with vigor!

269
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:18,355
Change of music!

270
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:20,399
What? Already?

271
00:23:20,899 --> 00:23:22,609
Donkey hits first! And a hook!

272
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:31,034
Wolf! What are you doing?

273
00:23:31,118 --> 00:23:32,828
The pigs are getting away!

274
00:23:33,787 --> 00:23:36,790
Reverse. Cue the music!

275
00:23:36,873 --> 00:23:38,250
Shit. Seriously?

276
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:39,876
What? Reverse?

277
00:23:40,377 --> 00:23:42,671
Wolf! You'd better run away quickly!

278
00:23:43,171 --> 00:23:45,465
All right, pigs, go!

279
00:23:50,053 --> 00:23:51,805
What the… Holy shit.

280
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:57,519
Where are you going, Wolf?
That's not the direction of the parade!

281
00:23:57,602 --> 00:23:58,562
Goddammit.

282
00:24:14,327 --> 00:24:16,329
I told you not to give Hyeok-jun
another job!

283
00:24:16,413 --> 00:24:18,790
He almost died.
And you sent him to his doom again?

284
00:24:18,874 --> 00:24:24,087
You're in league with those monsters,
aren't you? Die, you fucking devil!

285
00:24:30,093 --> 00:24:31,303
I go to church too.

286
00:24:40,437 --> 00:24:41,354
Ms. Ji-yoon.

287
00:24:42,564 --> 00:24:44,941
Calm down and listen to me.

288
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:50,238
Wasn't there a person
hanging around you and Mr. Hyeok-jun?

289
00:24:55,452 --> 00:24:56,286
This person.

290
00:24:58,079 --> 00:24:58,914
Wait.

291
00:24:59,706 --> 00:25:00,540
This is…

292
00:25:03,043 --> 00:25:05,212
This is that…

293
00:25:05,879 --> 00:25:06,755
The workers' acci--

294
00:25:06,838 --> 00:25:08,882
From the Workers' Compensation Service?

295
00:25:08,965 --> 00:25:10,008
That's right.

296
00:25:11,218 --> 00:25:14,095
That organization disbanded in the 1980s.

297
00:25:14,804 --> 00:25:16,640
This woman is not human.

298
00:25:17,849 --> 00:25:18,683
What?

299
00:25:24,397 --> 00:25:26,233
She's a monster from the other side.

300
00:25:34,991 --> 00:25:39,079
<i>Mr. Hyeok-jun is being used right now.</i>

301
00:25:41,790 --> 00:25:44,960
She's so meticulous
that she evaded the surveillance network.

302
00:25:45,460 --> 00:25:46,962
She's also very intelligent.

303
00:25:48,755 --> 00:25:50,715
I've dealt with many monsters until now,

304
00:25:51,299 --> 00:25:54,052
but I've never seen one
with such a complete sense of self.

305
00:25:56,763 --> 00:25:58,181
All right.

306
00:25:58,765 --> 00:26:02,352
I will take care of that monster.

307
00:26:02,435 --> 00:26:07,232
You go home and pray that your brother
finishes his part-time job safely.

308
00:26:16,491 --> 00:26:17,325
Ms. Byeon Ji-yoon!

309
00:26:47,272 --> 00:26:48,898
Holy shit.

310
00:27:15,884 --> 00:27:16,760
Oh shit.

311
00:27:22,265 --> 00:27:24,142
Excuse me, hey…

312
00:27:26,144 --> 00:27:27,228
Oh no.

313
00:27:28,438 --> 00:27:29,564
Take it off for me.

314
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:30,482
What?

315
00:27:31,775 --> 00:27:33,401
Take this off for me.

316
00:27:34,778 --> 00:27:36,571
Hold on.

317
00:27:54,005 --> 00:27:55,215
Wait.

318
00:28:00,053 --> 00:28:01,012
No way.

319
00:28:32,001 --> 00:28:34,838
Now, shall we begin the grand finale?

320
00:28:39,092 --> 00:28:43,221
You guys are getting closer
to becoming full-time employees.

321
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:56,568
Keep going until only one remains.

322
00:28:58,278 --> 00:28:59,112
That's it!

323
00:29:03,533 --> 00:29:04,367
Hi.

324
00:29:06,536 --> 00:29:07,370
Stop!

325
00:29:08,079 --> 00:29:11,291
A defective doll without its costume head
has appeared.

326
00:29:14,753 --> 00:29:16,838
Commence sanitation work!

327
00:29:24,554 --> 00:29:25,930
Stay away from me!

328
00:29:39,402 --> 00:29:40,695
No, wait!

329
00:30:05,845 --> 00:30:08,264
FANTASY HAUNTED HOUSE

330
00:30:08,348 --> 00:30:09,974
"FANTASY"

331
00:30:43,591 --> 00:30:47,345
Now, let's begin
Challenge! <i>A Father's Miracle!</i>

332
00:30:50,265 --> 00:30:56,187
A thrilling, heartwarming show
the whole family can enjoy together.

333
00:30:56,688 --> 00:30:59,065
What is the mission
the father must complete?

334
00:30:59,148 --> 00:31:02,986
The father's mission today is this!

335
00:31:08,074 --> 00:31:09,367
This is insane.

336
00:35:10,149 --> 00:35:14,070
Subtitle translation by: Yung Un Choi
